  "ingredients": [
    "2 large eggs",
    "0.5 cup milk",
    "0.5 cup water",
    "0.25 teaspoon salt",
    "1 cup all-purpose flour",
    "2 tablespoons butter, melted"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Whisk eggs, milk, water, and salt together in a large mixing bowl. Add flour and melted butter; whisk vigorously until batter is smooth and pourable.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/QyJyJXTp8KErCoOsqtgwcMnyZ2E=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/16383-basic-crepes-VAT-022-step-02-2c67ffb7850f4b4ab40205c098afec94.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/16383/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat a lightly oiled griddle or frying pan over medium-high heat. Pour or scoop the batter onto the pan, using approximately 1/4 cup for each crêpe. Tilt the pan with a circular motion so that the batter coats the surface evenly.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/gvk-j3-ZLSBGOGjMaauRknWmR3w=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/16383-basic-crepes-VAT-023-step-03-99bb3be41b434b40a571f3c3d579f0d0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/16383/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook until the top of the crêpe is no longer wet and the bottom has turned light brown, 1 to 2 minutes. Run a spatula around the edge of the skillet to loosen the crêpe; flip and cook until the other side has turned light brown, about 1 minute more.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/0plz2d-sw7tewQDth9OsQZhzxJM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/16383-basic-crepes-VAT-024-step-04-5d3e2064f3cc43bdbd44b3e2ace9ed65.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/16383/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve hot. Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
